@startuml
title COLORS Web Application - Class Diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class ColorsWebClient <<JavaScript>> {
    - userId : int
    - firstName : string
    - lastName : string
    + doLogin()
    + saveCookie()
    + readCookie()
    + doLogout()
    + addColor()
    + searchColor()
}

class LoginAPI <<PHP endpoint>> {
    + authenticate(login : string, password : string) : JSON
}

class AddColorAPI <<PHP endpoint>> {
    + addColor(color : string, userId : int) : JSON
}

class SearchColorsAPI <<PHP endpoint>> {
    + searchColors(search : string, userId : int) : JSON
}

class User <<database table>> {
    + ID : int
    + FirstName : varchar(50)
    + LastName : varchar(50)
    + Login : varchar(50)
    + Password : varchar(50)
}

class Color <<database table>> {
    + ID : int
    + Name : varchar(50)
    + UserID : int
}

ColorsWebClient ..> LoginAPI : sends login request
ColorsWebClient ..> AddColorAPI : sends add request
ColorsWebClient ..> SearchColorsAPI : sends search request

LoginAPI ..> User : queries
AddColorAPI ..> Color : inserts
SearchColorsAPI ..> Color : queries

User "1" -- "0..*" Color : owns

note on link
  Color.UserID logically associates each
  color with its owning user.
  The schema does not declare an explicit
  SQL foreign-key constraint.
end note

@enduml